	(text "Power: 20 V from the USB-C PD trigger module (Joy-IT ZY12PDN, set to 20 V) into J3.\n+20V goes straight to the coils (ribbon pin 26). D2 and the R-78E make 5 V for the Pico;\nD3 lets the Pico's own USB-C stay plugged in for flashing. NEVER 20 V on VSYS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b6fb6fd9-bbe6-5c28-adde-fe44e29e8feb")
	)
	(text "ESP32-S3-Pico pins: Raspberry Pi Pico numbering, see firmware/README.md.\nGND pins 8, 13, 18, 23, 28 and 33 are joined on the Pico itself and left unconnected here.\nPin 18 is next to the antenna, kept clear of copper."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.5 185.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cbdb865d-a226-50bb-967a-b23fb4182e65")
	)
	(text "Test points: Keystone 5000-series miniature loops."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.8 266.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "34ae82c8-5262-5a59-a00e-42ab73792b1b")
	)
	(text "10k pull-downs: hold every COL-SEL line and both strobes low while the ESP32 boots."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.8 226.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6aede1ca-4986-5d2e-bc10-f1e8f55de565")
	)
	(text "Ribbon pins 6 and 7 are crossed on the panel (6 = ROW2, 7 = ROW1).\nRibbon A feeds COL-SEL0-3, ribbon B COL-SEL4-7; everything else is shared."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.12 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e0e8ce42-d16a-5e51-8285-fa5cd5d56327")
	)
